  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe downward bias when recent history shows a downtrend followed by high volatility; forecasts consistently under-predict the magnitude of subsequent rallies.",
    "Forecasts fail to capture mean reversion after sharp spikes, resulting in significant overshoot errors where true outcomes reverse direction while models continue trending.",
    "Sentiment signals (0.20-0.40) often precede volatile regimes but are insufficient for the model to adjust its trajectory, leading to persistent underestimation of upside potential.",
    "The 30-day horizon is prone to 'trend persistence' errors; models extrapolate short-term momentum rather than accounting for regime shifts indicated by sentiment spikes and historical volatility.",
    "When recent history ends near a local minimum (e.g., <85), the model's flat-to-slowly-rising forecast fails to anticipate the explosive upward moves seen in true outcomes."
  ]
